shairport-sync-desktop (5.6.2-1) trixie; urgency=high

  * New upstream release 5.6.2:
    - Security fix: malformed DACP TLV tokens could cause out-of-bounds
      reads (GHSA-vfxr-hxq9-9h35).
    - 64-bit RTP timestamps on PTP connections, so AirPlay 2 sessions longer
      than about 12.5 hours no longer go silent.
  * Share the user units and the desktop default settings with the new RPM
    packaging (packaging/).

 -- Ari-Santa <apeach@live.no>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 18:21:18 +0100

shairport-sync-desktop (5.6.1-2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * AirPlay Receiver: add an Output picker. "Follow System" keeps AirPlay
    audio on the system default output; any other choice pins it to that
    device. Playing streams move immediately through PipeWire metadata; the
    saved pipewire.sink_target is applied by restarting the receiver once
    no sender is connected.

 -- Ari-Santa <apeach@live.no>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:50:22 +0200

shairport-sync-desktop (5.6.1-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: Shairport Sync 5.6.1 built for AirPlay 2 with NQPTP 1.2.9,
    both running as systemd user services in the desktop session, plus the
    AirPlay Receiver now-playing app.

